    Reduce the request relation over its tokens
    
    The request reduction starts with its token sumcheck: the claim is the equality-weighted sum of the token map at a token point, the sumcheck runs one equality weight per token bit, and the inner map rounds carry the equality factors of the later variables while the verifier weights the variable being bound. The general sumcheck also gains a sum-of-products summand over shown maps for the panel combinations of the layer relation. Focused tests compute the token claim by hand, prove and verify it, refuse a map whose sum does not match, and check the product-sum form.
    
    This is partial progress: the inner-dimension sumcheck, the stack and the row and affine claims are the next step.

